!** command file to create netcnf.mac for dn87 system **

.run mongen
*prompt
*net
*mon:netcnf.mac
*Y	; network software, please
*2	; two cpus
*2	; two dn87s
*0	; first one is one port 0
*2	; second one is one port 2 (It''s a long story why it''s not 1)
*0	; but no DN87Ss on cpu0
*0	; nor on cpu1
*1	; central site has to remain what users are used to (eg, MTA01x:)
*Mordor
*128	; pick a random number of remote ttys
*y	; network virtual terminals (for DECNET, that is)
*y	; support remote cdrs
*y	; support remote lpts
*n	; no remote data entry terminals
*n	; task to task
*140	; another random number for maximum number of connects
.mic return
